# Line endings. See #826.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is the Git-for-Windows default: it smudges LF -> CRLF on
# checkout while the index stays LF. Prettier defaults to endOfLine=lf, so
# `prettier --check` then fails on files nobody touched, and lint-staged's
# failure path restores the working tree (re-smudging CRLF) into a
# commit-blocking loop. Pinning eol=lf for tracked text types stops both.
#
# `.sh` matters beyond formatting: backend/scripts/predeploy.sh runs in the
# Linux backend image, where a CRLF shebang fails at exec.
#
# Deliberately narrow — one line per extension actually tracked here. The
# index is already LF for all of them, so this introduces no renormalization.
# Unity text assets (*.asset, *.meta, *.prefab, *.unity) are left to Git's
# auto-detection on purpose.

*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.jsx    text eol=lf
*.cjs    text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.mdx    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.svg    text eol=lf

# Binary types tracked in this repo — never line-ending-converted, never diffed.
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.avif   binary
*.mov    binary
*.wasm   binary
